# Product / UX standing preferences

- Use open source (or a reputable free tier of an OSS product) before building commodity systems: analytics, charts, email, CMS, search, observability.
- Custom code is for FindMyInvite-specific invitation experience, not Mixpanel clones.
- Keep `/akay` unlinked from public pages if it remains.
- Do not store analytics events in the guest invitations database.
- Hosts sign in with email and password to save a draft or publish. Forgot password is backlog; do not build it until Ashok asks.
- Operator Shortlist, Competitors, and Upcoming cards lead with a page preview of the existing http(s) link. Do not make those desks text-only.
- Gallery collection tabs are Premium, Elite, Free (not Royal/Classics). Premium v1.0: Sita Kalyanam, Velicha Poove, Rosu Rosu Rosu. Elite: remaining Royal designs. Free: all Classics. Retired assembly iterations stay off the gallery. The newest Premium clone is always the default Assembly parent.
- `/assembly` is a one-viewport mobile wizard: Pinterest URL → song → first/last opening stills → **Proceed to generate (Rs. 499)** → demo preview. No page scroll; next step by transition. Stills are free; video + site start only after that button. No payment gateway until Ashok asks. FIRST still: door fills the entire 9:16 frame; handle is the hero; materials/charms come from the pin.
- Premium cinematic clones: assemble locally (Approach B), then Ashok says **Publish**. Akay applies Supabase `template_catalog` SQL and commits/pushes `main`. Playbook: `documents/assembly-publish.md`. Ashok does not run SQL. Assembly UI shows preview links only (no file/migration dumps). Display names are editable before assemble.
